## Cloud Agent Infrastructure

### What is Cloud Agent?

Cloud Agent runs Cursor agents on Cursor-hosted virtual machines instead of your local machine. The agent:

1. Clones your repository into the cloud VM
2. Executes all tools (Read, Write, Shell, etc.) inside the VM
3. Returns results and generated changes back to your IDE
4. Can optionally auto-create pull requests

### Cloud vs Local Runtime Comparison

| Aspect | Cloud Runtime | Local Runtime |
|--------|--------------|---------------|
| **Execution location** | Cursor-hosted VM | Your machine |
| **Repo state** | Fresh clone, clean git state | Current working directory |
| **Network access** | Outbound internet enabled | Depends on local firewall |
| **Persistence** | Ephemeral (VM destroyed after run) | Persistent (your machine) |
| **Resource limits** | Defined by subscription tier | Your hardware limits |
| **Best for** | Long jobs, CI, PR creation | Quick edits, local debugging |
| **Agent ID prefix** | `bc-` | Non-prefixed |

