## Team Workspace Management

### Creating a Team

1. Go to [cursor.com/dashboard](https://cursor.com/dashboard)
2. Select "Create Team" or "New Workspace"
3. Name the team and set the organization identifier
4. Invite members via email or link

### Team Structure

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Cursor Account] --> B[Team/Workspace]
    B --> C[Team Members]
    B --> D[Team Settings]
    B --> E[Team API Keys]
    B --> F[Team Resources]
    
    C --> G[Admin]
    C --> H[Developer]
    C --> I[Viewer]
    
    D --> J[Shared Models]
    D --> K[Team Rules]
    D --> L[Team Skills]
    D --> M[Billing Preferences]
    
    F --> N[Shared MCP Servers]
    N --> O[Team Dashboard Servers]
```

### Team Roles

| Role | Permissions | Agent Access |
|------|------------|-------------|
| **Admin** | Full control, billing, member management | All features |
| **Developer** | Code access, agent runs, settings | All except billing |
| **Viewer** | Read-only access to project | Limited |

### Team Settings

Team-level settings override individual user settings for all team members:

```json
{
  // Team-level model configuration (all members use these)
  "team.agent.chatModel": "claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
  "team.agent.agentModel": "claude-opus-4-20250514",
  
  // Team-level API keys (inherited by all members)
  "team.provider.apiKey": "team_api_key_...",
  
  // Team-level custom instructions
  "team.agent.customInstructions": "Enterprise codebase. Follow OWASP guidelines.",
  
  // Team-level agent settings
  "team.agent.contextWindow": 200000,
  "team.agent.autoApprove": false
}
```

### Team Resources

| Resource | Shared? | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| **Team API keys** | Yes | Shared API keys for all team members |
| **Team rules** | Yes | `.cursor/rules/` in shared repo |
| **Team skills** | Yes | `.cursor/skills/` in shared repo |
| **Team MCP servers** | Yes | Dashboard-backed MCP servers shared across team |
| **Team agent runs** | Yes | Cloud agent runs billed to team account |

