## API Key Management

### Key Types

| Key Type | Scope | Usage |
|----------|-------|-------|
| **Personal API Key** | Individual account | Personal agent runs, cloud VMs |
| **Team Service Account Key** | Team workspace | Shared agent runs, CI/CD pipelines |
| **Admin API Key** | ❌ Not yet supported | — |

### Key Locations

```yaml
Personal Keys:
  URL: https://cursor.com/dashboard/integrations
  Scope: Individual user account
  Creation: Any team member with personal access

Team Service Accounts:
  URL: https://cursor.com/dashboard/teams/<teamId>/settings
  Scope: Entire team workspace
  Creation: Team Admin only
  Usage: CI/CD, shared automation, team services
```

### Key Management Best Practices

1. **Use service account keys for CI/CD**, not personal keys
2. **Rotate team keys** quarterly or after team member changes
3. **Never commit keys** to version control
4. **Use environment variables** in shared infrastructure
5. **Limit scope**: Service accounts should only have necessary permissions

```bash
# Personal key (not recommended for CI)
export CURSOR_API_KEY="cursor_personal_abc123"

# Team service account key (recommended for CI)
export CURSOR_API_KEY="cursor_team_xyz789"
```

